{"id": "EUVD-2026-93166", "enisaUuid": "c1c9c9f7-78f6-3f07-a343-f2116079688b", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: wwan: t7xx: validate the netif index in t7xx_ccmni_recv_skb()\n\nThe netif index carried in the DPMAIF PIT header is five bits wide,\nbut ccmni_inst[] only has room for NIC_DEV_MAX (21) entries.\nt7xx_ccmni_recv_skb() indexes the array without a bounds check, so\nindexes 21 to 31 read past it.  The out-of-bounds value lands in the\ncallback table that follows the array, which is never NULL, so the\nexisting !ccmni check does not catch it and the driver dereferences\nwhatever sits there as a struct t7xx_ccmni.\n\nDrop the skb when the index is out of range.\n\n\nVerified in a QEMU guest with a fault injector setting the netif\nindex to 25: the unpatched driver reads a value past ccmni_inst[],\nwhich lands in the callback table, and dereferences it far enough to\nqueue the skb.  With this check the packet is dropped.  Well-formed\ntraffic on index 0 is unaffected.\n\nChanges in v2: none.", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:45:09", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:16:09", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7c2fe308bda5a7e6222d7f0c3c311991372baab4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fba45070e25abdae08bcaebfadeef050dc39e208", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e1b0609b1a40da03e385be290853a604eb4c3fb9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9dbf13de4edff6fbc1f7ad9c4040326b6ed599ad", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d28aa2de9654e8024922775520a2665e00c04ad5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c7ead9704249d57d4693a04697e3bbd285138fa9"], "aliases": ["GHSA-wwj9-jxr5-39jp", "CVE-2026-98238"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "233c9d5f-05f5-3a0f-b3c6-76901f428a95", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "05d19bf500f8281f574713479b04679fa226d0a3 <7c2fe308bda5a7e6222d7f0c3c311991372baab4"}, {"id": "4380a950-4560-3a6a-a9cb-15a608744421", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.189"}, {"id": "587be395-0622-3942-8c80-a5fa623ce6f2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.54"}, {"id": "6ccfd1ea-db43-3c25-a9f9-17971197c7c9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "706d41dd-417f-3fa9-8cf0-d618a9c17e73", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "05d19bf500f8281f574713479b04679fa226d0a3 <9dbf13de4edff6fbc1f7ad9c4040326b6ed599ad"}, {"id": "81bc318b-d088-36c8-a17f-d7fbbb67ba99", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "05d19bf500f8281f574713479b04679fa226d0a3 <e1b0609b1a40da03e385be290853a604eb4c3fb9"}, {"id": "90e5d1c0-37fc-32ca-a483-b12984280c9c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "05d19bf500f8281f574713479b04679fa226d0a3 <fba45070e25abdae08bcaebfadeef050dc39e208"}, {"id": "9a186d08-fe17-383b-ba01-c22d806d2eac", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "9e6a1a28-41db-31cc-a39f-b26a4ea78121", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.8"}, {"id": "e1fb180e-5b5b-3b4a-a904-258d22f4dbcb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "05d19bf500f8281f574713479b04679fa226d0a3 <d28aa2de9654e8024922775520a2665e00c04ad5"}, {"id": "e52b1876-08a1-3d02-bed2-4d4aec9411e2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.19"}, {"id": "edc58dc9-495d-38f4-8639-33c5a576815a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "f48d0371-7b9b-3d46-bc6b-a9f06e9fb7aa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "05d19bf500f8281f574713479b04679fa226d0a3 <c7ead9704249d57d4693a04697e3bbd28